      "finding_id": "IPSEC-DH-001",
      "key": "IPSEC-DH-001|negotiated|dh_group|MODP-1024",
      "title": "Forbidden Diffie-Hellman group",
      "severity": "High",
      "category": "algorithm",
      "scope": "negotiated",
      "session_id": "vpn_c0a15c9a873db101",
      "rule_version": "1.0",
      "policy_id": "cnsa-strict",
      "evidence": {
        "parameter": "dh_group",
        "observed": "MODP-1024",
        "expected": "One of: MODP-3072, MODP-4096, MODP-6144, MODP-8192, ECP-384, ECP-521",
        "items": [
          {
            "packet": 2,
            "field": "isakmp.tf.id.dh",
            "value": "MODP-1024",
            "session_id": "vpn_c0a15c9a873db101"
          }
        ]
      },
      "why_it_matters": "MODP groups of 1536 bits or fewer give well under 112 bits of security. 1024-bit groups are within reach of well-resourced attackers through precomputation against common primes (the Logjam attack), which can expose the session keys, and RFC 8247 advises against them.",
      "remediation": "Use a 2048-bit or larger MODP group, or an elliptic-curve group, in the IKE proposal on both peers. A proposal that satisfies policy 'cnsa-strict': AES-256-CBC / HMAC-SHA2-384 / ECP-384 (strongSwan swanctl.conf: proposals = aes256-sha384-ecp384).",
      "standards": [
        "RFC 8247",
        "NIST SP 800-57 Part 1 Rev.5",
        "NIST SP 800-131A Rev.2"
      ]
    },
